Exercise: sa-network-review (chapter 12 lab)

Work on servera, with sudo or as root. Do not change the connection that
carries your SSH session (System enp5s0).

A static interface
 1. A NetworkManager connection named dummy1, type dummy, for the interface
    dummy1, with the static addresses 10.50.60.1/24 and 10.50.60.2/24, no
    IPv6, and the DNS server 10.50.60.53. Both addresses must be active now
    and stored in the profile.

Names
 2. A line in /etc/hosts that maps 10.50.60.1 to appnet.lab.example.com with
    the short alias appnet. Check it with getent hosts appnet.

On workstation
 3. Fill in answers.txt using what you see on servera (ip route, ss, and
    /etc/nsswitch.conf).

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-network-review
